WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.337 --> 00:00:02.454
- People who are, like,
super-villains or whatever,

00:00:02.454 --> 00:00:04.474
they always are depicted holding cats.

00:00:04.474 --> 00:00:05.542
That's nuts!

00:00:05.542 --> 00:00:08.504
How could you be compelled to
dominate the world right now?

00:00:08.504 --> 00:00:10.205
I never want to move again!

00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:13.133
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:14.034
(kittens mewing)

00:00:14.034 --> 00:00:16.508
Hello, I'm Hannah Hart, host
of Food Network's I Hart Food

00:00:16.508 --> 00:00:18.261
and today I'm going to be
answering your questions

00:00:18.261 --> 00:00:21.086
with some extra-special guests.

00:00:21.086 --> 00:00:23.454
♫ Let's just bring out the kittens

00:00:23.454 --> 00:00:24.954
Do we have babies?

00:00:26.008 --> 00:00:26.913
(gasping)

00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:28.150
Oh, hello!

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.714
Can we get more kittens?

00:00:29.714 --> 00:00:32.271
I actually have three cats in my lap.

00:00:32.271 --> 00:00:33.604
One, two, three.

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:37.328
The last one is asleep and he's hiding!

00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:40.943
I started out My Drunk Kitchen
as a joke for a friend.

00:00:40.943 --> 00:00:43.287
I was a proofreader working
at a translation firm.

00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:45.426
I had just moved from
San Francisco to New York

00:00:45.426 --> 00:00:46.807
and a friend of mine--

00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:49.140
Oh, he's so cuddly and warm!

00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:53.930
A friend of mine was going
through a little bout of

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:56.840
depression and I just wanted
to make a joke to cheer her up.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.645
I will have all the cats.

00:00:58.645 --> 00:01:01.446
We'll get every single kitten that's here.

00:01:01.446 --> 00:01:02.551
Ah, yes!

00:01:02.551 --> 00:01:04.949
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:08.742
I Hart Food is show that's
about going to different cities

00:01:08.742 --> 00:01:12.004
across America and seeing
how each of those areas

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:14.451
highlight local ingredients.

00:01:14.451 --> 00:01:16.883
How many ways can you cook a lobster?

00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:19.039
Isn't it all basically the same?

00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:21.201
That's something we explore.

00:01:21.201 --> 00:01:22.903
(smooching)

00:01:22.903 --> 00:01:25.414
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:01:25.414 --> 00:01:26.437
I think the best thing I ever made,

00:01:26.437 --> 00:01:29.907
well, I made souffle and
it wasn't that hard, guys,

00:01:29.907 --> 00:01:33.042
so that's all I have to say about that.

00:01:33.042 --> 00:01:34.192
And the worst thing I ever made?

00:01:34.192 --> 00:01:36.025
There's nothing, no regrets.

00:01:36.025 --> 00:01:38.104
I don't think you can
be an online creator,

00:01:38.104 --> 00:01:40.302
you know, I'm going six years strong,

00:01:40.302 --> 00:01:41.881
and I don't think you can
look back and think that

00:01:41.881 --> 00:01:44.416
you've made any big mistakes,
unless of course you did,

00:01:44.416 --> 00:01:45.484
and then you made an episode called

00:01:45.484 --> 00:01:46.740
My Drunk Kitchen: Whoopie Pie

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.103
where you explain that you're sorry.

00:01:49.103 --> 00:01:51.139
I say we do this for every interview.

00:01:51.139 --> 00:01:52.414
You guys like this?

00:01:52.414 --> 00:01:53.480
Choo-choo-choo-choo-choo!

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.798
Oh, my God, I think I like this!

00:01:54.798 --> 00:01:57.418
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:01:57.418 --> 00:02:00.458
No, restaurants are really
dangerous investments and

00:02:00.458 --> 00:02:02.955
I'm more of a
put-your-money-under-a-mattress
type of person

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:07.281
Now, would I ever consider
opening a cat cafe?

00:02:07.281 --> 00:02:08.761
Yes.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.594
Just be cool.

00:02:09.594 --> 00:02:10.560
Don't get too excited.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.721
This is the key to making content.

00:02:12.721 --> 00:02:15.806
You just let it happen
if it's gonna happen

00:02:15.806 --> 00:02:17.495
and if it's not?

00:02:17.495 --> 00:02:19.496
Oh, my God, oh my God, it's happening.

00:02:19.496 --> 00:02:20.756
All the kittens are here.

00:02:20.756 --> 00:02:22.683
Every kitten is here.

00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:24.673
It was here for a moment and now I believe

00:02:24.673 --> 00:02:26.496
that moment's captured in time.

00:02:26.496 --> 00:02:27.329
Forever!

00:02:27.329 --> 00:02:30.079
(dramatic music)

00:02:33.461 --> 00:02:36.082
(camera shutter clicking)

00:02:36.082 --> 00:02:39.513
(upbeat guitar music)

00:02:39.513 --> 00:02:43.084
I would say you're perfect
exactly as you are.

00:02:43.084 --> 00:02:44.917
You already know that.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.555
Don't let anyone teach you otherwise.

00:02:48.555 --> 00:02:50.003
Also, take as long as you need.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.856
I always feel like there's a
lot of pressure to come out

00:02:51.856 --> 00:02:53.894
but you should come out
when you're safe and sound.

00:02:53.894 --> 00:02:55.402
You know, when you feel
like you're in a physically

00:02:55.402 --> 00:02:57.052
and emotionally safe environment and

00:02:57.052 --> 00:03:00.091
you have a support group, then come out.

00:03:00.091 --> 00:03:01.546
Don't come out just
because people are saying,

00:03:01.546 --> 00:03:02.797
"Why aren't you coming out already?"

00:03:02.797 --> 00:03:03.630
Ugh!

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:04.971
Like, take as long as you need.

00:03:04.971 --> 00:03:07.362
It's your journey, nobody else's.

00:03:07.362 --> 00:03:11.172
You guys smell so fresh
and so clean-clean!

00:03:11.172 --> 00:03:12.640
Are you out, cats?

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.488
(giggling)

00:03:15.488 --> 00:03:17.032
Hi, do you like puns?

00:03:17.032 --> 00:03:19.046
If so, then you'll love I Hart Food.

00:03:19.046 --> 00:03:22.213
(upbeat guitar music)

00:03:24.425 --> 00:03:26.344
Yeah, Britney Spears was
a real inspo for that!

00:03:26.344 --> 00:03:28.426
(laughing)

00:03:28.426 --> 00:03:29.590
Right, you guys?

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:30.423
Look at this!

00:03:30.423 --> 00:03:31.256
Pa-pa-pa-pa!

00:03:31.256 --> 00:03:32.089
(gasping)

00:03:32.089 --> 00:03:32.922
What was it?

00:03:32.922 --> 00:03:33.755
What did you hear?

00:03:33.755 --> 00:03:34.588
What did your elf-eyes see?

00:03:34.588 --> 00:03:36.531
Did your elf-eyes see this bouncing ball?

00:03:36.531 --> 00:03:38.085
That's what I see!

00:03:38.085 --> 00:03:40.179
(upbeat guitar music)

00:03:40.179 --> 00:03:41.226
Definitely cats.

00:03:41.226 --> 00:03:45.309
I also believe in kittens
and puppies and babies.

00:03:47.094 --> 00:03:47.927
(gasping)

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:48.760
Hello?

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.744
♫ Hello, I love you

00:03:49.744 --> 00:03:53.559
♫ Won't you tell me your name

00:03:53.559 --> 00:03:55.256
♫ Yeah, it's Kitty

00:03:55.256 --> 00:03:56.089
Oh, bye, guys!

00:03:56.089 --> 00:03:57.244
They're not big fans of the oldies.

00:03:57.244 --> 00:03:58.523
I'll tell you that right now.

00:03:58.523 --> 00:04:00.300
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.312
Happiness means appreciating what you have

00:04:03.312 --> 00:04:06.078
and staying present in the
moment and not always thinking

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:08.416
about what you don't have.

00:04:08.416 --> 00:04:10.026
You're a baby!

00:04:10.026 --> 00:04:12.042
This is a baby!

00:04:12.042 --> 00:04:13.781
(kitten mewing)

00:04:13.781 --> 00:04:14.614
Too cute!

00:04:17.718 --> 00:04:18.704
I really like ASAPScience.

00:04:18.704 --> 00:04:20.459
I think that they're really
crushing it right now.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:21.292
Obviously, my friends.

00:04:21.292 --> 00:04:22.496
Grace, Mamie, Tyler.

00:04:22.496 --> 00:04:24.930
I think they're all hilarious.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.295
John Cozart, aka Paint!

00:04:26.295 --> 00:04:27.545
I really like Minute Physics.

00:04:27.545 --> 00:04:28.533
I don't know what he's
up to these days but

00:04:28.533 --> 00:04:30.276
Minute Physics was really great.

00:04:30.276 --> 00:04:31.109
Hello!

00:04:32.943 --> 00:04:34.243
See, he doesn't know that I'm really

00:04:34.243 --> 00:04:36.611
paying attention to him.

00:04:36.611 --> 00:04:40.213
He thinks that he's got
me but I've got him.

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:44.124
I just love answering this
man's questions over here.

00:04:44.124 --> 00:04:48.291
Definitely not trying to
get this kitten's attention.

00:04:49.977 --> 00:04:50.810
Is it working?

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.512
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:04:52.512 --> 00:04:54.501
I would say my go-to drink in college was

00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:57.002
whatever was available and-or nearby.

00:04:57.002 --> 00:04:58.497
In college, you really can't be picky,

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:01.435
but you can drink responsibly.

00:05:01.435 --> 00:05:04.127
(bell ringing)

00:05:04.127 --> 00:05:05.676
Malibu Coconut Rum.

00:05:05.676 --> 00:05:07.152
I don't think anyone
can drink that anymore

00:05:07.152 --> 00:05:08.491
because of college.

00:05:08.491 --> 00:05:10.505
♫ You're a little kitty

00:05:10.505 --> 00:05:12.642
♫ Cute and sweet

00:05:12.642 --> 00:05:16.622
♫ It's okay to go sleep-sleep

00:05:16.622 --> 00:05:18.659
♫ Yes you are a kitty

00:05:18.659 --> 00:05:20.643
♫ Every day

00:05:20.643 --> 00:05:22.552
♫ Yes you're a kitty

00:05:22.552 --> 00:05:24.520
♫ Hey, girl, hey

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:27.571
Just so you guys know, these
adorable kittens are all

00:05:27.571 --> 00:05:31.491
available to foster or adopt at the ASPCA.

00:05:31.491 --> 00:05:35.151
Go to ASPCA.org/fosterLA.

00:05:35.151 --> 00:05:38.560
Quick, before I just
take them all with me.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:41.643
(upbeat jazzy music)

